 ### Fixed

+- `OrchestratorHooks.onError` now fires on every rejection inside a turn, not only when the thrown value is an `Error` instance. A string, plain object, `undefined` or other non-`Error` value is wrapped in an `Error` with a readable `message` and the original value preserved as `error.cause`, while an `Error` instance reaches `onError` unchanged and the caller still receives the original rejection untouched. **Migration note**: if your `onError` hook counts failures or pages an operator, it will now also run for rejections that previously bypassed the `instanceof Error` check; read `error.cause` when you need the raw non-`Error` value.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).

